pan="1">Total</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">19</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">16</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Total per 10,000 bp</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">28.4</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">23.9</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">9.0</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="T4FN1"><label>a</label><p>Intergenic regions with reduced GC content are those with GC contents in the range of 46.3%-61.7%.</p></fn><fn id="T4FN2"><label>b</label><p>Local GC minima are those identified by visual inspection of the GC content trace as defined in a sliding 120 bp window as shown in Fig. (<bold><xref ref-type="fig" rid="F4">4</xref></bold>).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T5" position="float"><label>Table 5</label><caption><p>CA Repeat and TTAAAA Retrotransposition Insertion Sites in the HSV-1 Genome</p></caption><table frame="border" rules="all" width="100%"><thead><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Sequences</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Expected<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="T5FN1">a</xref></th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Observed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">CACACA (total)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">49</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">79</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">CACACA (in genes)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">39</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">55</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">CACACA (intergenic regions)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">10</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">24</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">TTAAAA (total)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">28</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">TTAAAA (in genes)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">18</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">TTAAAA (intergenic regions)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">10</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="T5FN1"><label>a</label><p>Statistically expected sequence numbers were calculated based on both strands of the 152,261 bp HSV-1 genome with 68% GC content. A 16%; T 16%; G 34%; C 34%. Calculated values were rounded to the nearest whole number. The proportions of gene and intergene regions in the HSV-1 genome were taken as 79% and 21%, respectively [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="R1">1</xref>, <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="R2">2</xref>].</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>